/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Sabarigiri Hydroelectric Power Project has been a key contributor to Kerala's energy needs since 1966, generating renewable energy while supporting local infrastructure and flood control. However, it has also caused significant environmental challenges, including forest submergence, biodiversity loss, and social displacement. Despite these trade-offs, the project highlights the need for better management practices, modernization, and community engagement to ensure sustainable development. Lessons learned from Sabarigiri, especially regarding environmental protection and infrastructure maintenance, will be crucial for the future of hydroelectric projects.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
